      "nota": "<p><strong>Location:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.IDd94316DhSx3ptV]{The Ferry Terminal and the Last Ferry}<br><strong>Scenes:</strong> @UUID[JournalEntry.doItxeK8y7M1PufU.JournalEntryPage.tG1m5PTkmBA1pvmc]{A4-E03 · The Last Ferry}</p>\n<p><strong>A4-E03, the car deck.</strong> “On the car deck, among the vehicles, there are few witnesses: normal Masquerade Difficulty.” It&#39;s the best place to fight: Dawson and the ghouls fight to protect the briefcase. <strong>Krell</strong>, if he survived and reached 3 steps in A3-E03, “shows up on the car deck to help David”; if not, he shows up to recover the folios, as a third force.</p>\n<p>Crop: the aft ~22 m of the deck (the rest of the boat continues forward: the strip along the west edge, behind a chain, isn&#39;t played). Along the sides, the <strong>casings</strong> (ventilation and machinery: you see their sheet-metal tops with the grilles; not played) with the starboard and port <strong>stairs</strong> up to the cabin (<code>ferry</code>). The <strong>cars</strong> are movable tiles (thirteen, in five lanes): they can be pushed, used as cover, and have their windows smashed; the Storyteller moves them or removes them.</p>\n<p><strong>The open stern.</strong> The deck ends at the <strong>stern chain</strong>; the center section unhooks when docking, and that&#39;s where the terminal&#39;s <strong>vehicle ramp</strong> comes in (the “Down the vehicle ramp” region, docked only: disable it on departure). Anyone who arrives late by car and reaches the ferry before it casts off comes in here. Jumping into the water from the open stern is a shorter drop than from the passenger deck (about 2 m), with the same swimming roll.</p>\n\n<p class=\"sbn-moviles\">The movable furniture (13) are unlocked tiles: they can be moved, knocked over or used as a barricade.</p>\n<div class=\"sbn-figuras\"><p><strong>Placed tokens.</strong> Hidden ones are revealed from the token layer; the ones that depend on how the night went say when.</p><ul><li>@UUID[Actor.Y53IKZpt8sl2sl65]{August Krell} · <em>hidden</em> (A4-E03): If he survived A3-E03: with 3 steps, he comes to help David; without them, to recover the folios.</li></ul></div>\n<p class=\"sbn-pendientes\"><strong>Exits without a map (grey region, leads nowhere):</strong> Jump into the water from the open stern.</p>",
      "moviles": []
    }
  },
